WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.290
Fill two identical balloons at
the same temperature and pressure.

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.630
One gets hydrogen.

3
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.270
The other gets carbon dioxide.

4
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.070
Hydrogen molecules are small and light.

5
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.250
Carbon dioxide molecules
are bigger and heavier.

6
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.410
Same size, same conditions,
very different molecules.

7
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.170
So which balloon holds more molecules?

8
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.690
In this mission, you'll
meet Avogadro's law,

9
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:30.270
and use it to predict the volumes in which gases
react, such as carbon monoxide burning in oxygen.

10
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.290
You'll use molar volume to turn a
gas volume into an amount in moles.

11
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.200
Your mission: decide which balloon
holds more molecules, and explain why.
